      <workList xml:id="workDesc_896e0b1e">
         <work xml:id="work_ide0704b6a">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_fc0c7fd3">C4:004</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_id79b01ebd" xml:lang="de">Erich Pontoppidans Versuch einer natürlichen Historie von Norwegen</title>
            <title type="original" xml:id="title_54deb0a6" xml:lang="da">Det første Forsøg paa Norges naturlige Historie</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_bab5e523">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_idc72fc240">Erik Pontoppidan</persName>
               <persName role="translator" xml:id="persName_7e5bdd1f">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_iddf8c39cf">
               <date enddate="1754" startdate="1753" xml:id="date_ee6c53cc">1753–54</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id1bc65f98">
               <p xml:id="idm151">In spring 1753 when Scheibe had finished the translation of <persName xml:id="idm152" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Caspar Peter Rothe</persName>’s biography on the Danish naval hero, <persName xml:id="idm153" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peter Tordenskjold</persName> (SchW C4:006), and dated the foreword, he began on <persName xml:id="idm154" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Erik Pontoppidan</persName>’s large work, <rend xml:id="idm155" fontstyle="italic">Det første Forsøg paa Norges Naturlige Historie</rend> (1752–53). As with other translations, it seems most likely that this one was commissioned by the publishers <persName xml:id="idm156" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Franz Christian Mumme</persName>. The first part of the book consisting of more than 400 printed pages appeared already the same year – that is in 1753; and the second part of around 600 printed pages was issued around half a year later. In his foreword to the translation of the first part, Scheibe also includes a list of earlier studies on the subject and mentions problems concerning the translation of some of the more obscure terms. Scheibe’s foreword to the second part consists mainly of comments regarding a critical review of his translation of the first part. He ends the foreword explaining as he does in other publications that 'the long distance and other circumstances did not permit me to send the proof-read sheets hither from Sønderborg.' (p. 36). Scheibe also remarked that his rather unreadable handwriting also adds to the number of printing errors. A lengthy review of the work appeared in<rend xml:id="idm157" fontstyle="italic"> Staats- und Gelehrte Zeitung</rend> (August 1753), mentioning that 'the German translation seems to have been made very hastily and the translator would probably also wish to have a greater knowledge of physics'. Part 1 was issued again in 1769.</p>
            </history>
